    vshort: [
      { q: "According to Taxonomy, under which kingdom do mushrooms fall?", a: "According to taxonomy, mushrooms fall under Kingdom Fungi." },
      { q: "What is a group of hyphae called?", a: "A group of hyphae is called Mycelium." },
      { q: "What is the umbrella-like part of a mushroom called?", a: "The umbrella-like part of a mushroom is called Pileus." },
      { q: "How many basidiospores are formed in a basidium?", a: "Four basidiospores are formed in a basidium after meiosis division." },
      { q: "What is the stalk of a mushroom called in English?", a: "The stalk of a mushroom is called Stipe." },
      { q: "Which cell division occurs in the life cycle of a mushroom?", a: "Meiosis division occurs in the life cycle of a mushroom." },
      { q: "By what other name is morel mushroom known?", a: "Morel mushroom is known by the name Morchella." },
      { q: "What percentage of sugar is used for drying mushrooms?", a: "6\\% sugar is used for drying mushrooms for storage." },
      { q: "Which vitamin is found in mushrooms?", a: "Vitamin B-Complex (B_1, B_2, B_{12}) is found in mushrooms." },
      { q: "What is dikaryotic mycelium?", a: "A secondary mycelium containing two nuclei in each cell is called dikaryotic mycelium." },
      { q: "Which part of the mushroom produces spores?", a: "The gills (Gills) of the mushroom produce spores." },
      { q: "What is the amount of cholesterol in mushrooms?", a: "The amount of cholesterol in mushrooms is zero." },
      { q: "How long should straw be cut for oyster mushroom cultivation?", a: "Straw should be cut into pieces of 1 to 2 inches." },
      { q: "What should be the temperature of the drying machine (Oven) for mushrooms?", a: "The temperature of the drying machine should be 40 to 45^\\circ\\text{C}." },
      { q: "What color are the gills of poisonous mushrooms?", a: "The gills of poisonous mushrooms are usually white." }
    ],
    short: [
      { q: "Explain the structure of the gills of a mushroom.", a: "Gills are the layered structures found under the pileus of a mushroom. They consist of three main layers: trama (inner), sub-hymenium (middle), and hymenium (outer). The basidium and paraphysis remain in the hymenium layer for reproduction." },
      { q: "Mention the nutritional value of mushrooms.", a: "Mushrooms are a rich source of protein (19-35\\%). They contain vitamins B_1, B_2, B_{12}, folate, and minerals like potassium, calcium, and iron. Being cholesterol-free, they are extremely beneficial for health." },
      { q: "Why is a mushroom called a saprophytic organism?", a: "Since mushrooms lack chlorophyll, they cannot perform photosynthesis. They obtain nutrition by absorbing organic food from dead and decaying organic matter, which is why they are called saprophytic." },
      { q: "Why is straw boiled in oyster mushroom cultivation?", a: "Straw is boiled for 15-20 minutes to destroy harmful germs, fungi, and bacteria, and to soften the straw so that the mushroom seeds can germinate and grow easily." },
      { q: "What is the process of making dried mushroom slices (sukuti) for storage?", a: "Mushrooms are cleaned, cut into pieces, and soaked in a solution of potassium bisulphide, citric acid, sugar, and salt for 16 hours, and then dried in a machine or under the sun to make dried slices." },
      { q: "How can poisonous mushrooms be identified?", a: "Poisonous mushrooms can be identified by characteristics such as having attractive colors, white gills, a ring (Volva) on the stipe, and showing a yellow color when the pileus is squeezed." },
      { q: "What is the economic potential of mushroom cultivation in Nepal?", a: "Commercial cultivation of oyster and button mushrooms in Nepal has created self-employment. Exporting high-value mushrooms like morels can earn foreign currency, showing that its economic potential is very high." },
      { q: "How is primary mycelium formed?", a: "When mature basidiospores produced in the basidium disperse through the air and land on a favorable place, they germinate and form a primary mycelium containing a single nucleus." },
      { q: "What is the medicinal value of mushrooms?", a: "Consuming mushrooms helps in fighting diseases like diabetes, cancer, and high blood pressure. Medicine made from red mushrooms is useful for asthma and piles patients." },
      { q: "What is the role of sterigmata in the life cycle of a mushroom?", a: "Sterigmata provide a pathway and support to transport the four nuclei formed by meiosis division inside the basidium to the developing basidiospores." }
    ],
